# Local Database Setup (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/technical/local-database-setup.md`. Local dev uses **docker
Postgres**; production uses **Neon** (ADR-013). Do NOT commit a real `.env`.

**First-time setup**
1. `cp .env.example .env.local` (or `.env`) and fill secrets (`AUTH_SECRET`, `SEED_OWNER_*`, provider keys). The local `DATABASE_URL`/`DIRECT_URL` defaults already match docker-compose.
2. `docker compose up -d` — start Postgres (port 5432, named volume `sr_app_pgdata`).
3. `npx prisma migrate dev` — apply migrations (uses `DIRECT_URL`).
4. `npx prisma db seed` — seed first OWNER (from `SEED_OWNER_*`) + representative data.
5. `npm run dev` — start the app.

**Common commands:** `docker compose down` (stop, keep data) · `docker compose down -v` (wipe data) ·
`npx prisma studio` (inspect) · `npx prisma migrate reset` (drop + re-migrate + reseed, local only).

**Rules**
- Never `prisma db push` against shared/prod — migrations only (see schema-change rule).
- Local defaults are dev-only credentials; production secrets live in the deploy platform.
- Keep the seed script **idempotent** (no-op if data exists) so re-runs are safe.
